# Drafted by Gemini (R26 Jinxed Leviathan), edited. The Jinxed Leviathan: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_leviathan_arrived
Narrator: Stilt shacks lean over Murkwater Bend where swamplights bob above sunken boats, and the wet air reeks of old luck gone sour.
check Wisdom DC 19 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: You keep your eyes on the warm brass glow of your own lantern, and the cold pale swamplights lose their pull.
set mf_leviathan_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: A pale glow coaxes {name} right off the slick planks, and they wade back up out of the duckweed, sodden and blinking.
damage 3d10 psychic party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: Every third plank groans or snaps beneath your boots, while the little lights out in the cypress knees wink like knowing eyes.
time +60
check Wisdom DC 19 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
mf_nadine_bayou [weary]: Nothing goes right in Murkwater this week, strangers. Boats sink at the rope, every roll comes up snake eyes, and something huge rolls in the dark water.
set mf_leviathan_asked
quest mf_leviathan asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
mf_nadine_bayou [weary]: Another flatbottom punt went down in dead calm water this morning, right at the post. Tell me you've learned something useful out there.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_leviathan_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
mf_nadine_bayou [weary]: Everything misses by an inch now. Knots slip, lanterns crack, the lights lead folk into the muck, and the revellers dance till their knees give out.
-> menu

~ where
mf_nadine_bayou [sad]: Old fools hexed a bull gator into a colossus of bad luck to spite Snake Eye Jack. It ate its makers first, and now itwallows in the deep pool.
-> menu

~ route_a
mf_nadine_bayou [neutral]: A great river serpent sacred to Jack's people nests upstream in the reeds. That gator hates it fiercely, and might follow if you drove it down.
* [Animal Handling DC 19] Bait the Leviathan with the sacred serpent -> a_ok | a_slow
* [Survival DC 19] Read the serpent's nesting place to lead the Leviathan -> a_ok | a_slow
* Drag bait through the swamp and see what follows -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
mf_nadine_bayou [smile]: Look there, the great serpent is sliding down the channel, and that wicked old gator is turning its snout to follow it home.
time +60
set mf_leviathan_found
set mf_leviathan_clue_a
quest mf_leviathan trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: It takes a long, sodden afternoon of cursed ropes and slipped footing, but at last the great bulk in the black water turns toward the deep pool.
time +300
set mf_leviathan_found
quest mf_leviathan trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_jack_follower [smile]: A fine damp evening for tempting fate, friends. Care to wet your whistles and drink to whatever luck you have left?
set mf_leviathan_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_jack_follower [neutral]: Back again, and still dry above the knees. Ask what you like, friends, the night isn't getting any younger.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_leviathan_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_leviathan_found and not flag.mf_leviathan_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_jack_follower [smile]: We bless little wooden idols of old Jack for good fortune. Turn a blessed idol on a hex-beast, and all its sour luck rebounds right down its gullet.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_jack_follower [sly]: I know the black hole where those witches brewed that beast, sure enough. Might even point you there, for a fair wager or a very convincing reason.
* [Intimidation DC 19] Intimidate him into telling where it was made -> b_ok | b_slow
* [Persuasion DC 19] Charm him into telling where it was made -> b_ok | b_slow
* Let him talk and listen to every wandering tale -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_jack_follower [sly]: They piled every spiteful hex they knew onto one mean gator, and it dragged them straight down to the black pool at the end of the rotten walk.
time +60
set mf_leviathan_found
set mf_leviathan_clue_b
quest mf_leviathan trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: It takes a long, bleary afternoon of spilled sour mash and crooked tales, but at last he points a wavering finger toward the black pool.
time +300
set mf_leviathan_found
quest mf_leviathan trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_jack_follower [smile]: What you need is an idol of Snake Eye Jack blessed by a true believer. Lucky for you, you're looking right at one.
* [Religion DC 19] Persuade him to bless an idol for you -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [Persuasion DC 19] Show proper reverence so he blesses it freely -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Pay your respects at the shrine and ask politely, over hours -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_jack_follower [smile]: Take this little carved fella and keep him dry. May Jack turn the bad dice back on the house, and may the swamp wink in your favour.
time +60
give mf_blessed_idol
set mf_leviathan_weak
quest mf_leviathan ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: It takes hours of quiet coin-tossing and muttered prayers beside the mossy shrine, but at last he presses the blessed wood into your palm.
time +300
give mf_blessed_idol
set mf_leviathan_weak
quest mf_leviathan ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: The rotten boardwalk gives out at the edge of a still, oil-black pool, with a low hump of mud and bleached ribs rising in its middle.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_leviathan_reveals
Narrator: The black water splits without a ripple, and the Jinxed Leviathan rises, a mountain of scarred hide crowned in tangled hex-charms and grinning wide.
cutscene mf_leviathan_reveals_2
Narrator: Its pale jaws yawn open, and a gust of river-rot and sour fortune washes over the planks.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_leviathan_weak
combat mf_leviathan_weak
elif level >= 18
combat mf_leviathan_full
else
combat mf_leviathan_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_leviathan_falls
Narrator: The great scarred bulk rolls belly-up and sinks into the black mire, out of luck at last, as the swamplights wink out one by one.
cutscene mf_leviathan_falls_2
Narrator: High above the cypress tops, the leering moon shifts her sour gaze south and west, toward a dark tangle of web-hung pines.
cutscene end
set mf_leviathan_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give tooth_of_the_jinxed_leviathan
quest mf_leviathan slain
xp milestone
Narrator: Deep in the Webwoods, a long needle pulls silver thread through the hush, and the lost children have gone very quiet.
-> END
